KPL/PCK

P_constants (PCK) SPICE kernel file mars_konopliv_2026_v1.tpc
===========================================================================

   By: Nat Bachman (NAIF)    2026 October 3

   PCK for Mars rotation, based on data from the 2026 publication
   by Konopliv et al. [1].

   To assist with PCK interoperability, rotation data for Phobos and Deimos, 
   and triaxial ellipsoid shape models for all three bodies, are included.
   These data are from sources [2] and [3]. 

   This kernel was created with the assistance of Claude Sonnet 5.


Sources and References
--------------------------------------------------------

   Sources and background references for the constants listed in this
   file are:

        [1] Alex. S. Konopliv, Ryan S. Park, Sebastien Le Maistre, 
            Marie Yseboodt, and Rose-Marie Baland, "Updated Mars 
            Orientation and Gravity Field and Indication of Decadal 
            Changes in Rotation Rate." The Planetary Science Journal, 
            2026, DOI: 10.3847/PSJ/ae9ba7.

        [2] Archinal, B.A., Acton, C.H., A'Hearn, M.F., Conrad, A.,
            Consolmagno, G.J., Duxbury, T., Hestroffer, D., Hilton,
            J.L., Kirk, R.L., Klioner, S.A., McCarthy, D.,
            Meech, K., Oberst, J., Ping, J., Seidelmann, P.K., Tholen,
            D.J., Thomas, P.C., and Williams, I.P., "Report of the IAU
            Working Group on Cartographic Coordinates and Rotational
            Elements: 2015," Celestial Mechanics and Dynamical Astronomy
            130, Article number 22 (2018).
            DOI: https://doi.org/10.1007/s10569-017-9805-5

        [3] Archinal, B.A., Acton, C.H., Conrad, A., Duxbury, T.,
            Hestroffer, D., Hilton, J.L., Jorda, L., Kirk, R.L.,
            Klioner, S.A., Margot, J.-L., Meech, K., Oberst, J., 
            Paganelli, F., Ping, J., Seidelmann, P.K., Stark, A.,
            Tholen, D.J., Wang, Y., and Williams, I.P., "Correction to:
            Report of the IAU Working Group on Cartographic Coordinates
            and Rotational Elements: 2015."


   Rotation data for Phobos and Deimos, and triaxial ellipsoid 
   radii for all three bodies, are included. These data are from 
   [2] and [3].


Toolkit Compatibility Warning
--------------------------------------------------------

   This file provides Mars system rotation data usable with the
   N0067 and newer versions of the SPICE Toolkit. This file cannot 
   be used to compute Mars, Phobos, or Deimos orientation with 
   Toolkit versions N0066 or earlier versions. See "Software Limitations" 
   below.

   All other data are compatible with the N0066 and earlier Toolkits.

   NAIF provides the PCK file 

      mars_konopliv_2026_n0066_v1.tpc 
      
   for use with older Toolkits. That PCK contains all the data from this 
   file, except that, in that file, one of the phase angle polynomials
   for Phobos is truncated to first order.


Software Limitations
--------------------------------------------------------

   SPICE support for quadratic phase angle polynomials was introduced 
   in the N0067 Toolkit version. Older Toolkits cannot make use of the 
   Mars system orientation data provided in this file. 
   
   Older Toolkits are unable to detect and signal a SPICE error if
   they are used to compute orientation of Mars, Phobos, or Deimos
   using these data: memory corruption will occur in user applications
   linked to these Toolkits if the applications attempt such computations.
   Any results, including those of unrelated computations, may be invalid
   after such memory corruption occurs.

   See the NAIF server at

      https://naif.jpl.nasa.gov

   for the file mars_konopliv_2026_n0066_v1.tpc, which can be used 
   with older Toolkits.


Kernel Interoperability
--------------------------------------------------------

   This PCK file can be safely loaded after other, older 
   generic text PCKs created by NAIF. Loading it before 
   these or other text PCKs may prevent use of Mars system 
   rotation models from those files.

   PCK incompatibility can be due to kernel variables defined 
   by this PCK and not overwritten by PCKs loaded later.

   This problem can be resolved in two ways: 

      1) After using this kernel, unload it before loading 
         incompatible PCKs.
       
      2) After using this kernel, load the PCK 

            mars_rotation_reset_v1.tpc 

         before loading incompatible PCKs. Loading that file after 
         this PCK has been used, and before another PCK is loaded, 
         enables Mars system rotation models from the last-loaded 
         PCK to function properly.

         See the documentation within mars_rotation_reset_v1.tpc 
         for details.
  

Data Modifications
--------------------------------------------------------

   1) Poisson terms in the angular expressions for alpha, delta, and W 
      in the source model have been replaced by asymptotic approximations, 
      in order to represent the expressions in a format compatible with 
      SPICE Toolkit software. 

      The approximation replaces expressions of the form

         T * sin ( a + b * T )
         T * cos ( a + b * T )

      with, respectively, sums of expressions of the form

         constant * scale * sin( T / scale ) * sin ( a + b * T )
         constant * scale * sin( T / scale ) * cos ( a + b * T )

      Here T represents Julian centuries past J2000 TDB, and 
      
         scale = 1.0e4

      The modified expressions agree with the original ones,
      over the time range 1970-2050, to these levels:

         Maximum absolute alpha error (rad) = 5.33e-15
         Maximum absolute delta error (rad) = 6.66e-16
         Maximum absolute W error     (rad) = 1.09e-10

      These errors were determined by sampling using a step size of 
      approximately 250 seconds. 

      The modified expressions have been analytically transformed
      to expressions that satisfy SPICE text PCK requirements.

   2) A typo in a constant in pck00011.tpc has been corrected. 
      The quadratic coefficient in the 5th Mars system phase angle 
      has been set to 

         12.71192322

      replacing the value from pck00011.tpc 

         12.711923222

 
